      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks. yeah, it's just so frustrating. i feel like i'm constantly being picked at by these little things. \n\nyou mentioned they're like \"sneaky little pests\"—it literally feels like there's something lurking in the background of my account, just waiting to grab a few cents here and there when i'm not looking. do you think it's just bad luck, or is there actually something harder to catch than just regular fees? like, why do they always seem to hide in the shadows of the statement?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It's more than just bad luck; it's often a deliberate strategy by the merchants or services, which is much trickier to catch than a straightforward, large bill. These hidden charges are often designed to be so small that you don't notice them until they've accumulated into a significant amount—like a slow, persistent infestation of tiny, sneaky little things. Sometimes, these are just poorly named recurring charges, but sometimes they can be outright fraudulent activity, which is far more alarming than a simple subscription.\n\nIf you're worried about something truly lurking in the shadows, you might want to check your bank's security alerts or consider setting up transaction notifications. Those alerts are like having a lookout guard watching the perimeter, so you catch the little gremlins the moment they try to sneak in. Regular, large fees are easy to spot, but these micro-charges require you to be actively hunting for them, which is exhausting!",
      "source": "target",
